index b2db5375..136b0ba6 100644
--- a/docs/api.rst
+++ b/docs/api.rst
@@ -438,7 +438,24 @@ All loaders are subclasses of :class:`BaseLoader`.  If you want to create your
 own loader, subclass :class:`BaseLoader` and override `get_source`.
 
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.BaseLoader
-    :members: get_source, load
+    :members: get_source, load, add_alias, remove_alias,
+        resolve_template_name
+
+Built-in loaders provide ``add_alias(alias, target)`` and
+``remove_alias(alias)``. Aliases and targets are strings. Normal loading
+resolves one mapping on its owning loader before source access or
+composite routing; children resolve their own mappings independently.
+Aliases never chain within one loader. Missing targets report their
+target name with :exc:`TemplateNotFound`, including prefixed names.
+
+Replacing or removing an alias invalidates it in each Environment that
+has loaded it, without removing unrelated cached names. Ordinary
+template names remain distinct Environment cache entries. Listing keeps
+direct targets and adds aliases whose one-step target is in the ordinary
+listing; broken or chained aliases do not create extra entries. A loader
+without ordinary enumeration still raises its existing ``TypeError``.
+Custom subclasses retain their source and loading extension protocol and
+do not need to call the BaseLoader initializer merely to keep working.
 
 Here a list of the builtin loaders Jinja provides:
 
